🚽 Test case: legacy_void() is a legacy/untyped export (STDROT_ANY)
🚽 whose actual runtime result is STDROT_NONE (void). Used as a bare
🚽 statement that's fine -- but used where a value is expected
🚽 (`gigachad x = legacy_void();`), the semantic analyzer has no static
🚽 type for it to reject statically (infer_expression_type() reports
🚽 NONE, so the declaration check is skipped outright), so
🚽 evaluate_expression_double() must catch it at runtime instead of
🚽 silently treating "no value at all" as 0.0.
skibidi main {
    gigachad x = legacy_void();
    bussin 0;
}
